00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:49.859
The original villain for the movie, who ended
up being deleted, was a character called Miss

00:00:49.859 --> 00:00:50.859
Guffin.

00:00:50.859 --> 00:00:54.960
In an earlier version of the film, Miss Guffin
was Poppy's mentor and an elder Troll who

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.309
was kidnapped by the Bergen Chef.

00:00:57.309 --> 00:01:01.059
And in a twist in the story, it would have
been Miss Guffin who betrayed Poppy and the

00:01:01.059 --> 00:01:05.530
other trolls later in the film, rather than
Creek who ends up as the turncoat troll in

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:07.070
the final film.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:10.820
Trolls movie producer Gina Shay said that
Miss Guffin was set up to be "so appealing

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:13.640
and funny that nobody could recover when she
turned evil."

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:17.670
Although Miss Guffin was cut from the movie,
the character wasn't completely lost though

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:22.100
as her design was reused for Grandma Rosiepuff,
Branch's grandmother.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:27.479
You'll remember that Grandma Rosiepuff appeared
in Branch's flashback scene where she sacrificed

00:01:27.479 --> 00:01:32.030
herself to save Branch when he accidentally
drew the Bergens' attention because of his

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:33.030
singing.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:37.340
Grandma Rosiepuff is voiced by YouTuber, GloZell
Green, and as a nice easter egg to that the

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.430
character has green lips and hair.

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:43.310
Another deleted character from the movie was
the master yogi Cybil.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:47.731
After Creek became a more significant character
in the film, Cybil was sadly cut, although

00:01:47.731 --> 00:01:52.310
as art director and character designer Timothy
Lamb explained "a lot of [Cybil's] yoga [and]

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:55.400
Zen elements [were] incorporated into Creek's
character".

00:01:55.400 --> 00:02:00.450
Although the Trolls movie made its first official
casting in 2014 with Anna Kendrick in the

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:05.070
role of Princess Poppy, the film's history
is much more complicated and goes all the

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:10.640
way back to 2001 when DreamWorks Animation
bought the rights to adapt author Terry Pratchett's

00:02:10.640 --> 00:02:14.130
The Nome Trilogy, aka The Bromeliad Trilogy.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:18.660
And in 2008, they attached Slumdog Millionaire
director Danny Boyle as the director of the

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:23.030
planned adaptation, but that was abandoned
due to the economic crisis at the time.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:28.750
The project was restarted in 2010 with a new
director and a new title, Trolls, and was

00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:32.670
set to combine the Trolls toys with some elements
of Terry Pratchett's novel.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:36.760
Both Chloe Moretz and Jason Schwartzman had
been cast as leads by this point, but the

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:40.260
story had changed so much that their casting
was no longer a good fit.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:44.720
So, the film was completely recast starting
with Anna Kendrick and the following year

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:48.480
in 2015, Justin Timberlake joined to voice
Branch.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:54.170
Satin and Chenille, also known as "The Fashion
Twins" and voiced by Swedish electropop duo

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:57.870
Icona Pop, were originally going to have a
running joke through the movie where they

00:02:57.870 --> 00:02:59.940
changed their clothes in every scene.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:04.160
For example, after being captured by the Bergens,
they would have reappeared dressed in prison

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.570
clothes, like an orange jumpsuit.

00:03:05.570 --> 00:03:10.470
However, the filmmakers ended up abandoning
the idea as it would have been very expensive!

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:14.930
The giraffe-like Cooper is one of the most
distinctive trolls in the Troll Village and

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:19.060
the inspiration for his design came from a
set of "animal"-type trolls that character

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:23.110
designer Timothy Lamb discovered while researching
the history of Troll toys.

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:27.530
But before the filmmakers settled on Cooper's
final design which we see in the movie, initial

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:31.950
concept art showed him as a mailman and a
tap-dancing giraffe.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:36.330
When the villainous Bergen, Chef, finds Poppy
and the trolls during her celebration party

00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:40.970
in the theatrical release, Poppy is dressed
in her normal clothing; however, in the same

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:44.830
scene in the trailers, she's wearing what
looks like a ceremonial robe.

00:03:44.830 --> 00:03:49.180
This change suggests Poppy was going to be
made queen much earlier in the story rather

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:51.030
than at the very end of the film.

